# L §2.3 Calls: "a.b(x) for a member's (§6.1)"; L §2.4 Expressions (tally 2.1.4, issue #80): "none before a call's
# `(`, its prefixes and a band's key included". A joint model's ask calls its member's band, a.fee(a.income[a.ana]),
# and reprints so, touching. Was `a.fee (a.income[a.ana])`, which no parser reads back: every joint model with a
# member's band call failed to reprint.
=== options reprint
=== J/joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "../A/ana.tally" sha256 "71199adf94c4e5b296f8a2a329994846c0bf935d86860bb2726beeecec6ea41e"

ask f: a.fee(a.income[a.ana]) law 2026-06-30
